Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: marvell: linksys: enable both switch CPU links

The Armada 385 Linksys boards connect switch port 5 to the SGMII MAC
and port 6 to the RGMII MAC. OpenWrt disabled the former when switching
to DSA because multiple CPU ports were not supported and that MAC did
not have a bootloader-provided address.

Restore the port 5 link in the shared Linksys description, keeping the
existing port 6 connection. Conduit assignment is userspace policy.

---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/marvell/armada-385-linksys.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/marvell/armada-385-linksys.dtsi
@@ -116,7 +116,7 @@
 };
 
 &eth2 {
-	status = "disabled";
+	status = "okay";
 	phy-mode = "sgmii";
 	buffer-manager = <&bm>;
 	bm,pool-long = <2>;
@@ -198,6 +198,17 @@
 				label = "wan";
 			};
 
+			ethernet-port@5 {
+				reg = <5>;
+				phy-mode = "sgmii";
+				ethernet = <&eth2>;
+
+				fixed-link {
+					speed = <1000>;
+					full-duplex;
+				};
+			};
+
 			ethernet-port@6 {
 				reg = <6>;
 				phy-mode = "sgmii";
